{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Elohim saw the light that it was good, and He separated.</b> Here too we need the words of aggadah: He saw that it was not fit for the wicked to use, and set it apart for the righteous in the time to come. And according to its plain sense, interpret it thus: He saw that it was good, and it is not proper for it and for darkness to be used in mixture, so He fixed the boundary of this one in the day, and of this one in the night."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:02.733472721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}